1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,100
A goalkeeper's high kick.

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:03,603
A friend's flat throw.

3
00:00:03,603 --> 00:00:05,165
A jump over a puddle.

4
00:00:05,565 --> 00:00:07,818
Some stay in the air for ages.

5
00:00:07,818 --> 00:00:09,687
Some land almost at once.

6
00:00:09,687 --> 00:00:10,964
What decides it?

7
00:00:11,414 --> 00:00:15,071
Aarav tested it in the college
corridor with a soft ball.

8
00:00:15,421 --> 00:00:19,513
He threw it at thirty degrees,
then at sixty, with the same speed.

9
00:00:19,513 --> 00:00:21,184
Which one stays up longer?

10
00:00:21,684 --> 00:00:23,517
Most people guess, the same.

11
00:00:23,517 --> 00:00:26,180
Let's find the exact
answer, and the reason.

12
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:28,642
So what is the time of flight?

13
00:00:28,992 --> 00:00:33,514
It is the total time a projectile stays
in the air, from leaving to landing.

14
00:00:33,914 --> 00:00:37,103
Here, it lands back at the
same height it started from.

15
00:00:37,503 --> 00:00:41,699
The key idea: only the up and
down motion decides when it lands.

16
00:00:41,699 --> 00:00:44,083
The sideways motion just comes along.

17
00:00:44,733 --> 00:00:48,912
Let's throw two balls in our motion
notebook, with the same speed, twenty

18
00:00:48,912 --> 00:00:50,113
metres per second.

19
00:00:50,463 --> 00:00:52,990
The blue ball goes at thirty degrees.

20
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:55,567
The violet ball goes at sixty degrees.

21
00:00:55,967 --> 00:00:59,299
Watch the two clocks, and the
graph of height against time.

22
00:00:59,699 --> 00:01:03,408
The thirty degree ball lands
first, after about two seconds.

23
00:01:03,808 --> 00:01:05,443
Slow motion at the top.

24
00:01:05,443 --> 00:01:08,972
The violet ball is at its
top at half its flight time.

25
00:01:08,972 --> 00:01:11,501
Going up takes as long as coming down.

26
00:01:12,001 --> 00:01:16,067
The sixty degree ball lands after
about three and a half seconds.

27
00:01:16,067 --> 00:01:20,239
A steeper throw has a bigger
upward part, so it stays up longer.

28
00:01:20,889 --> 00:01:23,877
Now let's find the formula,
one step at a time.

29
00:01:24,227 --> 00:01:25,142
Step one.

30
00:01:25,142 --> 00:01:30,789
Up and down, y equals v naught sin
theta times t, minus half g t squared.

31
00:01:31,539 --> 00:01:32,439
Step two.

32
00:01:32,352 --> 00:01:35,623
When the ball lands, it
is back at height zero.

33
00:01:35,623 --> 00:01:37,209
So put y equals zero.

34
00:01:37,959 --> 00:01:38,959
Step three.

35
00:01:38,959 --> 00:01:41,317
Take t out as a common factor.

36
00:01:41,317 --> 00:01:45,631
t times, v naught sin theta
minus half g t, equals zero.

37
00:01:46,381 --> 00:01:47,281
Step four.

38
00:01:47,242 --> 00:01:51,739
So either t is zero, which is the
launch, or the bracket is zero.

39
00:01:52,489 --> 00:01:54,852
The bracket gives the landing time.

40
00:01:54,852 --> 00:01:57,744
T equals two v naught sin theta, over g.

41
00:01:58,544 --> 00:01:59,609
Remember this.

42
00:01:59,609 --> 00:02:03,711
Time of flight depends only on
the upward part of the velocity.

43
00:02:04,411 --> 00:02:07,478
Let's check it a second way,
using the top of the path.

44
00:02:07,828 --> 00:02:12,716
Going up, the upward speed falls by g
every second, from v naught sin theta

45
00:02:12,716 --> 00:02:13,794
down to zero.

46
00:02:14,194 --> 00:02:18,220
So the time to reach the top
is v naught sin theta, over g.

47
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:22,724
Coming down takes the same time,
so the total is twice that.

48
00:02:22,724 --> 00:02:24,912
Two v naught sin theta over g.

49
00:02:24,912 --> 00:02:26,152
Both ways agree.

50
00:02:26,802 --> 00:02:27,894
Side by side.

51
00:02:27,894 --> 00:02:30,807
At thirty degrees, sin theta is one half.

52
00:02:30,807 --> 00:02:34,821
T is two times twenty times a
half, over nine point eight.

53
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:36,166
About two seconds.

54
00:02:36,566 --> 00:02:40,715
At sixty degrees, sin theta is
about zero point eight seven.

55
00:02:40,715 --> 00:02:43,271
T is about three point five seconds.

56
00:02:43,871 --> 00:02:44,904
Now you try.

57
00:02:44,904 --> 00:02:46,188
Same speed again.

58
00:02:46,188 --> 00:02:49,288
Which angle gives the
longest time in the air?

59
00:02:49,288 --> 00:02:50,572
Pause and decide.

60
00:02:53,772 --> 00:02:54,933
Ninety degrees!

61
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:55,938
Straight up.

62
00:02:55,938 --> 00:02:59,036
Sin ninety is one, the biggest sin can be.

63
00:02:59,036 --> 00:03:01,243
So T is two v naught over g.

64
00:03:01,893 --> 00:03:03,244
Here is a surprise.

65
00:03:03,244 --> 00:03:05,854
Look at what is missing from the formula.

66
00:03:06,204 --> 00:03:08,090
There is no cos theta in it.

67
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:11,188
The sideways speed does
not change the time at all.

68
00:03:11,588 --> 00:03:12,488
Your turn.

69
00:03:12,450 --> 00:03:17,392
From one table top, a ball is dropped,
and another is pushed off sideways.

70
00:03:17,392 --> 00:03:18,709
Which lands first?

71
00:03:18,709 --> 00:03:19,927
Pause and think.

72
00:03:23,127 --> 00:03:24,027
Together!

73
00:03:23,889 --> 00:03:27,651
Both start with zero upward
speed, and the same gravity.

74
00:03:27,651 --> 00:03:30,490
The push only makes one land farther away.

75
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:32,876
Now, one worked example.

76
00:03:33,226 --> 00:03:37,948
A ball is kicked at nineteen point six
metres per second, at thirty degrees.

77
00:03:37,948 --> 00:03:39,813
How long is it in the air?

78
00:03:40,313 --> 00:03:42,933
The upward part is v naught sin theta.

79
00:03:42,933 --> 00:03:47,486
Nineteen point six times one half,
nine point eight metres per second.

80
00:03:48,236 --> 00:03:51,957
Time to the top is nine point
eight, over nine point eight.

81
00:03:51,957 --> 00:03:53,289
That is one second.

82
00:03:54,039 --> 00:03:56,141
The time of flight is twice that.

83
00:03:56,141 --> 00:03:57,041
Two seconds.

84
00:03:57,670 --> 00:03:59,136
Now, the exam trap.

85
00:03:59,486 --> 00:04:04,109
Many students write T equals v
naught sin theta over g, and stop.

86
00:04:04,459 --> 00:04:07,068
But that is only the time to the top.

87
00:04:07,068 --> 00:04:09,311
The ball still has to come down.

88
00:04:09,311 --> 00:04:10,932
Always multiply by two.

89
00:04:11,582 --> 00:04:12,867
Where is this asked?

90
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:17,325
You find the time of flight, or work
back from it to the speed or the angle.

91
00:04:17,925 --> 00:04:19,108
Exam level now.

92
00:04:19,108 --> 00:04:23,708
A ball is in the air for four
seconds, and lands eighty metres away.

93
00:04:23,708 --> 00:04:24,608
g is ten.

94
00:04:24,590 --> 00:04:26,805
Find its launch speed and angle.

95
00:04:26,805 --> 00:04:28,037
Pause and solve.

96
00:04:33,437 --> 00:04:34,762
The answer is A.

97
00:04:34,762 --> 00:04:38,662
Twenty root two metres per
second, at forty five degrees.

98
00:04:39,162 --> 00:04:42,105
T equals two v naught sin theta over g.

99
00:04:42,105 --> 00:04:46,928
So v naught sin theta is four times
ten over two, which is twenty.

100
00:04:47,428 --> 00:04:52,448
Sideways, eighty metres in four seconds
means v naught cos theta is twenty.

101
00:04:52,448 --> 00:04:57,170
Both parts are twenty, so theta is
forty five degrees, and v naught is

102
00:04:57,170 --> 00:04:58,436
twenty root two.

103
00:04:59,036 --> 00:05:00,494
Here is your recap.

104
00:05:00,494 --> 00:05:01,994
Screenshot this card.

105
00:05:05,194 --> 00:05:08,030
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

106
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:09,330
One.

107
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:12,576
Why does the sideways speed
not change the time of flight?

108
00:05:13,476 --> 00:05:14,376
Two.

109
00:05:13,954 --> 00:05:16,230
Why is there a two in the formula?

110
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:18,030
Three.

111
00:05:17,710 --> 00:05:21,190
Which launch angle keeps a
ball in the air the longest?

112
00:05:22,290 --> 00:05:25,450
Next time: the ball turns
at half its flight time.

113
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:27,668
But how high is that turning point?

114
00:05:27,668 --> 00:05:29,408
Find out in maximum height.
